+# Selector diagnosis
+
+Completion criterion: one agent-runnable diagnostic command reproduces the epoch-200 FULL-arm anchor selections and emits, for all ten fixed anchors, (1) the zero-interaction selection, (2) exact/model/selector fixed-panel scores, (3) score components by size and checkpoint, (4) signed per-pair interaction error and its size implication, (5) no-op invariance, (6) label evaluation accounting and singleton convention, and (7) the cached third-order residual R3; the root report states which causal explanations each result supports or rejects.

