V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:7:**Scope of this run.** Evaluation worlds ['V025_PROBE/world/3']; 5 anchor steps x nearest-eligible carrier only; learner seeds ['V025_LEARNER/seed/1', 'V025_LEARNER/seed/2'] (2); learned arms ['FULL', 'DROP_C3'] plus BASELINE, S0, S_UNI; checkpoint epoch 200 (NOT the sealed 2000); training rows restricted to `rows/world-1` (first 5 anchor shards).
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:22:PILOT_NOT_CLAIM. **Training is also inherited from the earlier full-scale run and was not re-executed here.** The minimal pilot restores the **epoch-200** checkpoint (2 seeds x {FULL, DROP_C3}); the sealed budget is 2000 epochs and was deliberately *not* used.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:24:Learned arm-seed lineages ran with concurrency 16; external BASELINE seed records were emitted separately. Neutral batches were hoisted once per worker. Each learned lineage completed 2000 source epochs with a checkpoint every 100 epochs; **this report evaluates the epoch-200 checkpoint**.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:50:- Escape/harm counts by selected coalition size: {'2': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '3': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '4': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '5': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '6': {'escape_opportunities': 2, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '100': {'escape_opportunities': 5, 'selected': 10, 'harmful': 2}}.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:74:- Escape/harm counts by selected coalition size: {'2': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '3': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '4': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '5': {'escape_opportunities': 3, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '6': {'escape_opportunities': 2, 'selected': 0, 'harmful': 0}, '100': {'escape_opportunities': 5, 'selected': 10, 'harmful': 2}}.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:85:The C2 tie-break diagnostic is the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose C2 head score is exactly equal to the incumbent's under the FULL arm, i.e. C2 cannot discriminate the move and the ranking falls through to C1 plus the stable configuration-ID tie-break. `c2_tie_frequency` is the fraction of anchor-seed decisions with any such tie; `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` is the mean per-decision tie fraction. See DEFECTS.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:111:- **D-MIN-3 (suspicious result). `FULL` selects the all-users coalition (size 100) at every anchor-seed.** `escape_and_harm_by_coalition_size` shows `selected: 10` at size 100 and `selected: 0` at every size 2-6, while positive-joint escape opportunities exist at sizes 2-6. A selector that always moves all 100 users is far more likely to be an artefact of the epoch-200 head's scale than a real decision. Two of those ten selections were harmful by exact joint delta (harmful-acceptance rate 0.2).
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:112:- **D-MIN-4 (internal inconsistency). `V_CA` is large and negative while `FULL` pooled EE is the highest of all arms.** Net `V_CA` is -1.365e11 bit-equivalents (bits -1.222e10, -eta*energy -3.373e10, Phi -9.054e10) against the additive selector, yet `FULL` pooled EE (3.425e7) exceeds `DROP_C3` (2.352e7), `S0` (1.759e7) and `BASELINE` (1.699e7). Either the `V_CA` reference (the additive selector) or the pooled-EE aggregation is not measuring what the schema intends. **This must be resolved before any V_CA number is reported at scale.**
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:114:- **D-MIN-6 (scope). Arms `DROP_C1`, `DROP_C2` and `ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL` were skipped** to fit the time budget, as the minimal-pilot brief permits. Their epoch-200 checkpoints exist in `artifacts/v025-pilot-min-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM/checkpoints/` and can be added by widening `PILOT_ARMS`.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:122:- Stage-C build 3 imported `coalition_identity`, absent from the stage-4d target snapshot. A compatibility implementation restored both exact B4 identities and accepts uncapped selected coalitions.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:130:- V_CA and coalition-size anti-pattern strata were not first-class build-3 receipt fields. The pilot records V_CA as the realised FULL-minus-additive-selector F difference, with bits, -eta*energy and Phi components unclipped, and emits explicit size strata.
V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:134:- Exhaustive exact interaction decomposition over every catalogue row was also unbounded. Exact Psi is computed for every P-u joint escape candidate and every selected FULL coalition; other rows retain learned scoring only. P-u top-10 users are primitive-ranked by |d_i^u|. The pilot S_UNI wall budget was reduced to 5 seconds, with the engine's fallback and termination certificate retained verbatim.
