.scratch/chinese-word-v023-lcsrs-20260905-r2/en/bilingual/bi-mc-modqn-base.md:259:Here $J_1(\cdot)$ and $J_3(\cdot)$ are the Bessel functions of the first kind of orders 1 and 3, and $2.07123$ is that equation's fixed angle argument, the same value that appears in other multibeam-satellite work. $F$ is naturally unity at $\theta=0$ ($1/4+3/4$), so no extra boresight normalization constant is required, however $J_1(\mu)/(2\mu)$ and $36J_3(\mu)/\mu^{3}$ are $0/0$ at $\mu=0$, so the limit is taken directly whenever $|\mu|<\epsilon_\mu$, with $\epsilon_\mu$ given in Section 5.1. $\theta_{3dB}$ is a fixed antenna parameter, but it appears on the right-hand side of the definition of $\mu$ and, through $\mu$, sets the shape of $F$ and $G^{T}$, it is therefore listed as an argument of all three, so that the left-hand side of every definition covers the quantities that appear on its right. $G_0$ is different: it is a multiplicative scale constant that does not change the shape of the pattern and is therefore not an argument. From Eq. (3.10) onward the same function is applied at a specific link's off-axis angle, so it is written with the fixed parameter explicitly as $G^{T}(\theta_{u,s,v},\theta_{3dB})$. This layer does not introduce a three-index gain variable and does not add a pattern selector.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-screen/ADJUDICATION-OUTSIDE-ROUND3-C3S-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-2026-09-08.md:66:   「同態residual診斷固定為首rung第一個預定world、全部lineages、steps 0–29；commit後以隔離的predecision-state clone及相同keyed realised field，比較selected action與該C3-S state的BASE proposal。報nominal／realised ΔB、ΔE、Δserved、Δ(B−η_refE)及其差，不拿另一臂state代替。不得回饋selector、調參或rescue；無可驗證state則報不可得。」
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-C3-FUTURE-PATH-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-07.md:20:Two corrections matter: R7 **already tested a named two-player coalition**, and [PNFE already included future offsets](/home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover/src/mcrl/runtime/ee_axis_pnfe.py:1). Untested alternatives are broader action-set coordination, different deployment rules, and adaptive branch trajectories—not “coalitions” or “longer horizons” without qualification. New anchor regimes also remain untested; favorable-regime hunting is forbidden.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-C3-FUTURE-PATH-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-07.md:72:1. **OPS-3 action-set coalition value.** Shared circuit/baseband charges and last-user beam shutdown create complementarity. For a prospectively defined occupancy component and joint proposal \(C\),
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-C3-FUTURE-PATH-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-07.md:79:   where \(\phi_u\) is a fixed coalition allocation, such as Shapley allocation, and \(d_{12,u}\) is the declared C1/C2 contribution in bits. The interface must expose the proposed action set. R7’s selected two-player equal-share residual does not exhaust this mechanism. **Falsifier:** the fixed joint catalog lacks EE/service headroom, or its learned additive deployment fails composition. Reuse F0 accounting and coalition identities; add joint profiles and explicit partial-adoption checks.
.scratch/chinese-word-v023-lcsrs-20260905-r2/en/mc-modqn-base.en.md:194:Here $J_1(\cdot)$ and $J_3(\cdot)$ are the Bessel functions of the first kind of orders 1 and 3, and $2.07123$ is that equation's fixed angle argument, the same value that appears in other multibeam-satellite work. $F$ is naturally unity at $\theta=0$ ($1/4+3/4$), so no extra boresight normalization constant is required, however $J_1(\mu)/(2\mu)$ and $36J_3(\mu)/\mu^{3}$ are $0/0$ at $\mu=0$, so the limit is taken directly whenever $|\mu|<\epsilon_\mu$, with $\epsilon_\mu$ given in Section 5.1. $\theta_{3dB}$ is a fixed antenna parameter, but it appears on the right-hand side of the definition of $\mu$ and, through $\mu$, sets the shape of $F$ and $G^{T}$, it is therefore listed as an argument of all three, so that the left-hand side of every definition covers the quantities that appear on its right. $G_0$ is different: it is a multiplicative scale constant that does not change the shape of the pattern and is therefore not an argument. From Eq. (3.10) onward the same function is applied at a specific link's off-axis angle, so it is written with the fixed parameter explicitly as $G^{T}(\theta_{u,s,v},\theta_{3dB})$. This layer does not introduce a three-index gain variable and does not add a pattern selector.
