.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-chatgpt-review-package-20260908/PROMPT-CHATGPT-DEEP-RESEARCH.md:6:1. **Literature on credit assignment / reward shaping for cooperative multi-agent control that separates "learnability" from "alignment/factoredness"**: COIN & difference rewards (Wolpert–Tumer; Agogino–Tumer), Wonderful Life Utility, counterfactual baselines (COMA), marginal contribution / Shapley-based rewards, potential games and smoothness, coordination graphs / factored value functions, mean-field and "team reward vs local reward" tradeoffs. Which of the package's target families are instances of these (PNFE ≈ difference reward? coalition residual ≈ two-player marginal contribution? CSE/EC ≈ cost-share rules?), and what does the literature say about **when such per-agent externality signals fail to improve the global objective** (e.g., non-additive global objectives such as ratios; strong coupling where beneficial events are multi-agent coordination events; scale mismatch when shaping terms are added to value estimates; one-step counterfactuals under multi-step dynamics)?
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-chatgpt-review-package-20260908/00-README.md:5:Read in this order: `01-CHRONOLOGY.md` (eight C3 designs and their sealed stop tokens), `02-R7-STOP-PHYSICS-RESULT.md` (the full LC-SRS gate result with per-world numbers), `03-F1-KILL-SCREEN-RESULT.md` (+ `03b-F1-r2-receipt.json`, `03c-F1-ULTRA-ADJUDICATION.md`), `04-CONTINGENCY-LADDER.md` (the pre-outcome D/F design), `05-R7-CONTRACT.md` (§5–§8: predicates, one-shot rule, what a later experiment must declare), `06-COMPOSITION-RULING.md` (why C3 enters as Q1+Q2+z/κ), `07-C1C2-SUCCESSOR-DECLARATION.md` (what is sealed and proceeding without C3), `08-F3-DESIGN-R2.md` (the unlaunched learner-screen design), `09-PRIOR-DESIGN-ADJUDICATIONS/` (V0.14 STOP_THREE_HEAD, V0.15 REJECT, V0.15-R FAIL, V0.20 repriced-C3 rulings), `10-PHYSICS-AND-CODE/` (`step.py`, `link_budget.py`, `ee_axis_coalition_residual_c3.py`, `c3_contingency_f0.py`, F1 runner + tape format, target generator excerpt), `11-HANDOFF-SECTIONS.md` (§13 R7, §17 C3 decision, §2 root causes).
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3-chatgpt-review-package-20260908/00-README.md:9:Key numbers: R7 — learner balanced accuracy 0.705 vs placebo 0.626 (PASS); physics 11-vs-00 pooled EE −0.049%, 2/8 worlds positive (FAIL → `STOP_PHYSICS_R7`); learned composition −0.660% vs baseline, teacher +0.335%; topology consistency 0.536. F1 (world 2026121721, lineage 2026092101, 2 steps, 100 users) — BASE 118,630,258 bits/J; D 117,054,987 (−1.33%, service 0.995 < 0.999); F 113,248,876 (−4.54%) → `FAST_SCREEN_NO_SUPPORT`. V0.20 — exact coalition residual +0.985% EE at λ′=1.03η, nominal 2/3 lineages.
